    "walkthroughs": [
      {
        "id": "swcraftFirstHour",
        "title": "The first hour with SWCraft",
        "description": "Find the panel, onboard a project, edit the model with schema help, run the authoritative gate, read the generated diagrams, talk to the model through the agent, and open the guide that came with your install.",
        "steps": [
          {
            "id": "findThePanel",
            "title": "Find the SWCraft panel",
            "description": "SWCraft has its own Activity Bar icon — the strip of icons down the far edge of the window — and three sections under it: Model, Experiments (with the Allocation (CARMA) experiment and Trace Links) and Setup, which folds away once the project is set up. Help sits in the `…` at the top of the SWCraft view. If you cannot see the icon, the strip has pushed it into the `…` overflow at its foot.\n[Show the SWCraft view](command:workbench.view.extension.swcraft)",
            "media": {
              "markdown": "media/walkthrough/01-panel.md"
            },
            "completionEvents": [
              "onView:swcraftView"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "onboardProject",
            "title": "Onboard a project",
            "description": "Point SWCraft at a folder. It runs `swcraft init` if there is no `swcraft.yaml` yet and copies in the agent profile — after checking that the installed `swcraft` actually runs. The MCP server needs no file: this extension registers it.\n[Onboard Project](command:swcraft.onboardProject)",
            "media": {
              "markdown": "media/walkthrough/02-onboard.md"
            },
            "completionEvents": [
              "onCommand:swcraft.onboardProject"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "editALayerFile",
            "title": "Edit a layer file",
            "description": "One element per file, under the layer directories in `model_root`. The bundled JSON Schemas give you completion, hover and per-file diagnostics through the Red Hat YAML extension the pack installs.",
            "media": {
              "markdown": "media/walkthrough/03-edit.md"
            },
            "completionEvents": [
              "onContext:swcraft.activeEditorIsLayerFile"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "validate",
            "title": "Build — the gate",
            "description": "`SWCraft: Build` runs what `moon run :build` runs — clean the outputs, check the model, generate the ARXML, the diagrams and the requirements — and ends with `swcraft validate`, which checks the ARXML it generated. The editor's red squiggles are usability assistance; `swcraft validate` is the authoritative gate, and it sees everything a single-file schema cannot.\n[Build](command:swcraft.build)",
            "media": {
              "markdown": "media/walkthrough/04-validate.md"
            },
            "completionEvents": [
              "onCommand:swcraft.build"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "seeTheDiagrams",
            "title": "See the model as diagrams",
            "description": "`SWCraft: Diagrams` generates the model's diagrams — an internal block diagram and an overview per composition, the nesting of the compositions, the deployment of the tasks on the cores (when the model declares a task) and a sequence diagram per scenario — into `views_root`, and shows their index page in a tab of the editor, with pan, zoom and search; Ctrl+click (Cmd+click on macOS) on a drawn element opens its YAML file beside the diagram. A saved change marks them out of date; press Diagrams again to see it.\n[Diagrams](command:swcraft.diagrams)",
            "media": {
              "markdown": "media/walkthrough/05-diagrams.md"
            },
            "completionEvents": [
              "onCommand:swcraft.diagrams"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "talkToTheModel",
            "title": "Talk to the model",
            "description": "Open Copilot Chat, pick **SWCraft Architect** from the chat-mode dropdown, and ask for a change. The agent reaches the model only through the SWCraft MCP server, and the first call of each tool asks permission — answer *Allow in this Workspace* once. This step ticks when the Chat view opens; the conversation itself happens where SWCraft cannot see it.\n[Open Copilot Chat](command:workbench.action.chat.open)",
            "media": {
              "markdown": "media/walkthrough/06-agent.md"
            },
            "completionEvents": [
              "onCommand:workbench.action.chat.open"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "openTheGuide",
            "title": "Open the user guide",
            "description": "The whole guide came with your install. **Open Guide**, in the `…` at the top of the SWCraft view, serves it on this machine and shows it inside VS Code, in an editor tab — search and navigation included, no network needed, and it describes the release you actually have rather than whichever one is newest.\n[Open Guide](command:swcraft.openGuide)",
            "media": {
              "markdown": "media/walkthrough/07-guide.md"
            },
            "completionEvents": [
              "onCommand:swcraft.openGuide"
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "languages": [
      {
        "id": "xml",
        "extensions": [
          ".arxml"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "yamlValidation": [
      {
        "fileMatch": [
          "swcraft.yaml"
        ],
        "url": "./schemas/manifest.schema.json"
      },
      {
        "fileMatch": [
          "**/swc/**/*.yaml"
        ],
        "url": "./schemas/swc.schema.json"
      },
